menu "Smart-Air AI Scheduler"

    config SA_AI_ENABLED
        bool "Enable on-device CO/NO2 early warning (publishes ai/state; see SA_AI_CONTROL_RELAY)"
        default n
        help
            Strictly opt-in for the first hardware bring-up (see
            ai/gas_ews/README.md). When disabled, ai_scheduler_start() is a
            no-op: no task is created, no relay/buzzer/MQTT calls are ever
            made. sensor_task still feeds gas_ews (a few float ops per poll).

    config SA_AI_CONTROL_RELAY
        bool "Let the AI switch the Fan relay and buzzer (otherwise observe-only)"
        depends on SA_AI_ENABLED
        default n
        help
            When disabled (default), the AI only publishes
            device/{id}/ai/state and never touches the relay or buzzer.
            Calibrate the GM702B/GM102B first (preheat >= 24h, then
            calibrate_co / calibrate_no2): an uncalibrated GM102B reads ~2 ppm
            NO2 in clean air, close to the QCVN STEL of 5.3 ppm. Run
            observe-only for a few days and check ai/state before enabling.

            When enabled, the AI only ever switches OFF a Fan it switched ON
            itself -- a Fan switched on by a user is never switched off by
            the AI. Buzzer: 3 short beeps on early warning, 5 long beeps
            when a QCVN limit is exceeded.

    config SA_AI_FAN_ON_LEVEL
        int "Switch the Fan on from this level (1 = early warning, 2 = limit exceeded)"
        depends on SA_AI_CONTROL_RELAY
        default 1
        range 1 2
        help
            1: ventilate as soon as the early warning predicts a QCVN STEL
            exceedance within 10 minutes (earlier, more Fan runtime).
            2: only once STEL or TWA is actually over the limit.

    config SA_AI_FAN_RELAY_CHANNEL
        int "Relay channel the AI controls (1-based)"
        depends on SA_AI_ENABLED
        default 1
        range 1 3
        help
            Per the app's own channel labeling (relay_1=Fan, relay_2=Lamp,
            relay_3=Filter -- see app/lib/screens/devices/
            device_dashboard_screen.dart), the AI should control the Fan
            channel (default 1). Only ONE channel is ever touched by AI.

    config SA_AI_OVERRIDE_COOLDOWN_MIN
        int "Minutes to back off after an external relay change (minutes)"
        depends on SA_AI_ENABLED
        default 30
        range 1 240
        help
            Whenever a Fan the AI switched on is found switched off
            (detected by polling relay_get_all(), no changes to
            relay.c/mqtt.c needed), the AI scheduler assumes a human (app
            tap) or another controller just took over, and stays hands-off
            on that channel for this many minutes before resuming automatic
            control. device_mode OFF is not counted as an override.

endmenu
